    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing... there isn't a \"temporary\" version of this. it's not just a bad day, it's just the reality of my life. you talk about a \"respite\" but what if the only way to actually stop the noise and the weight is to just... stop? like, why is staying the only \"right\" answer? it feels like people just say that because they're scared of the alternative, not because it's actually a good reason to keep suffering. if everything is just a cycle of performing and hurting, isn way out actually a",
